    "at_runspecpollutantprocess": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/chain-so2-co2e-mechanism/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecpollutantprocess.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecpollutantprocess"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "27 rows, and they are THREE different kinds of thing. Three carry a rate of their own -- 101 (THC) off `emissionratebyage`, 601 (N2O) and 9101 (Total Energy) off `emissionrate`. Twenty are computed by SCALING another: 501 and 7901 at chain depth 1 off 101, 8001 and 8701 at depth 2, the fourteen toxics at depth 3, and 3101 and 9001 at depth 1 off 9101. Three are computed by SUMMING several -- 8601, 8801 and 9801 -- and have no multiplicative parent at all. The twenty-seventh, 300001, is the mechanism pseudo-pollutant 3000: selected, and emitting nothing. This is the only place the run's pollutant/process scope is written down; it comes from here and never from the RunSpec XML. It is not an output-block axis either: the output relation is ranked globally over the rate relation because the blocks are 125, 124, 104, 64 and 0 rows (docs/esm-conventions.md 31).",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "at_runspecchainedto": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/chain-so2-co2e-mechanism/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecchainedto.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecchainedto"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope",
          "chain"
        ],
        "note": "21 rows over three levels off THC -- 501 and 7901 <- 101, 8001 and 8701 <- 7901 and 101, the fourteen toxics <- 8701 -- plus 3101 <- 9101, and TWO rows for 8601. MOVES's own statement of which pollutant-process is computed by scaling which other one, read rather than written down.\n\nIT IS NOT A COMPLETE STATEMENT OF THE CHAIN, and that is finding F41. Only `AirToxicsCalculator` reads this table in MOVES; `HCSpeciationCalculator` has no ChainedTo table at all, and `CO2AERunningStartExtendedIdleCalculator` and `TOGSpeciationCalculator` carry their input pollutants as Java constants. So 9001, 9801 and 8801 have no row here even though all three are chained, and the document unions this table with the one calculator constant it needs. The 8601 pair is the other half of the same asymmetry: two rows for one output, which the parent join would sum into the nonsense id 8501 if `rspp_isSummed` did not hold it out.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "at_methanethcratio": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/chain-so2-co2e-mechanism/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__methanethcratio.parquet"
      },
      "reader_options": {
        "float_columns": [
          "CH4THCRatio"
        ]
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_methanethcratio"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "speciation"
        ],
        "note": "140 rows, all processID 1: `HCSpeciationCalculator`'s first lookup (hcspeciation.rs:663-679). Keyed by (processID, fuelSubtypeID, regClassID) and BANDED on model year, and NMHC is `THC x (1 - CH4THCRatio)`. Methane itself -- `THC x CH4THCRatio`, pollutant 5 -- is not selected by this RunSpec, so the complement is the only thing read out of this table. The KEY is on the fuel SUBTYPE, so the county's supplied formulation decides it: gasohol E10 (12), not conventional gasoline (10). There is no fuel subtype 90 row, and MOVES's lookup is an inner one, so an electricity cohort produces no NMHC -- and, because VOC comes from the same `speciate_emission` call, no VOC either, and no toxic chained off it. That single miss is all five species blocks' twenty missing cohorts.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "at_hcspeciation": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/chain-so2-co2e-mechanism/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__hcspeciation.parquet"
      },
      "reader_options": {
        "float_columns": [
          "speciationConstant",
          "oxySpeciation"
        ]
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_hcspeciation"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "speciation"
        ],
        "note": "272 rows over TWO output pollutant-processes, 136 each for 8001 (NMOG) and 8701 (VOC): `HCSpeciationCalculator`'s second lookup (hcspeciation.rs:596-618). The table is keyed by the OUTPUT pollutant-process, so the join on `rt_polProcessID` both finds the constants AND identifies which rate rows are NMOG or VOC rows -- neither pollutant is named anywhere in this document, and NMOG needed no new equation when the table gained its 8001 rows. Keyed further by fuel subtype, regClass and a model-year band. `oxySpeciation` is 0 on all 272 rows, so lib/adjustments.esm's `speciation_factor` never leaves its constant here; the term is written because the source writes it and docs/chain-so2-co2e-mechanism.md records that it is untested.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "at_altcriteriaratio": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/chain-so2-co2e-mechanism/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__altcriteriaratio.parquet"
