          "chain"
        ],
        "note": "27 rows -- the execution database's copy is filtered to the run's own pollutants, one per `runspecpollutantprocess` row -- read for TWO columns. `globalWarmingPotential` is the SQL's `CO2EqPollutant` extract (co2ae:1116-1131) and it is a nullable SMALLINT: 1 on Atmospheric CO2, 28 on methane, 265 on N2O and NULL on the other 24, so it is listed in `float_columns` and the NULLs arrive as NaN (docs/esm-conventions.md 11).\n\nMEASURED ACROSS THE CORPUS, and it is the size of this rung: the 42 snapshots' `pollutant` tables union to 116 distinct pollutantIDs with a maximum of 3000, and NONE of CB05's 1000 to 1018 appears in any of them. `calculator-dag.json` credits `TOGSpeciationCalculator` with 184 registrations, which are those sixteen pseudo-pollutants plus NonHAPTOG across twelve organic-gas processes. Against this database it registers 24 pairs and writes exactly one pollutant, 88. docs/chain-so2-co2e-mechanism.md 0.3 has the measurement.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
