      "type": "integer",
      "default": 2767,
      "description": "THE ONE DECLARED NUMBER IN THIS DOCUMENT: how many (pollutant-process, cohort) pairs reach MOVESOutput, over all six pollutant-processes together. 644 = 124 THC + 5 x 104 species, and it is ONE number rather than a per-block cohort count BECAUSE THE BLOCKS ARE NOT THE SAME SIZE (docs/esm-conventions.md 31). The twenty electricity cohorts have no `methanethcratio` row for fuel subtype 90, MOVES's lookup is an inner one, and every species block is those twenty cohorts shorter than the parent's. So the rank is GLOBAL over the rate relation: `rt_outputRank` numbers the emitting rate rows 1..644 by an inclusive prefix count and the output row joins to that rank, which needs no block to be rectangular. WHICH rows emit is a result of the chain and is never written down; `run_outputRateRowCount` recomputes 644 from it and `pp_emittedCohortCount` recomputes 124 and the five 104s per pollutant-process -- 129 + 103 x 5 is 644 too."
    },
