        "zmh_heatIndex": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "zonemonthhour_rows"
          ],
          "description": "`ZoneMonthHour.heatIndex`, COMPUTED from `temperature` and `relHumidity` rather than read back off the reference: MeteorologyGenerator.doHeatIndex MG-3, ported as lib/meteorology.esm's `heat_index` and specified in docs/meteorology-generator.md 2.2. It is the dry-bulb temperature below 78 degF and the National Weather Service regression capped at 120 degF at or above it.\n\nThe run's hour is 7, at 59.500000000000 degF, so the sub-78 arm is what reaches `run_heatIndex` and the computed value is the temperature BIT FOR BIT -- which is why this retarget moves not one byte of this fixture's MOVESOutput (docs/esm-conventions.md 23, docs/meteorology-generator.md 8.2). Over all 24 rows the computed column agrees with the reference's stored one to 7.93e-15 relative, 17 of them bit-identical."
        },
