            "rate_rows",
            "operating_mode_rows"
          ],
          "description": "J22: ONE clause carrying six key pairs, and THIS IS A COST DECISION, not a reading order (docs/esm-conventions.md 25). Splitting it into one-pair clauses gives a byte-identical answer and, measured on mixed-onroad's 164 x 60 version of it, takes 43x as long. The pollutant-process pair is now a column of the rate relation rather than a run-level scalar, which is what keeps the composite gate a composite gate at 492 x 60 output cells."
        },
        "rt_hasFlatRate": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Does `emissionrate` carry a row for this rate row's source bin? Six key pairs where the age-keyed lookup has seven: energy and N2O do not deteriorate, so there is no age group to match and every model year of a source bin shares one rate."
        },
        "rtMode_flatRate": {
