        "evTemperatureSourceTypeCeiling": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 40.0,
          "description": "adjust.rs:114. The heat-index suppression applies to source types below 40, i.e. light duty. Source type 21 qualifies, so the suppression is REACHABLE here and is decided by the heat index alone."
        },
        "evTemperatureSuppressionHeatIndex": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 67.0,
          "description": "adjust.rs:114. This run's heat index is 59.5 degF, 7.5 degF below the threshold, so the suppression does NOT fire and the EV quadratic is live. `mixed-onroad`'s margin is 0.0999985 degF (docs/esm-conventions.md 37.2); this fixture is not the tight one."
        },
        "evTemperatureReferenceDegF": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 72.0,
          "description": "adjust.rs:108. The EV branch's reference temperature is 72 degF where the standard quadratic's is 75. Both are written because both are reached: THC takes the 75 arm and electricity energy takes the 72 one, in the same document and at the same hour."
        },
        "run_evTemperatureIsSuppressed": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "run_rows"
          ],
          "description": "adjust.rs:113-115: light duty above a heat index of 67 degF has its AC usage set by the heat index rather than by this cold term, and the adjustment is dropped. 59.5 is below 67, so it is NOT suppressed here and the quadratic below reaches an emitted number -- unlike `mixed-onroad`, where the same code is a no-op at hour 9."
        },
        "rt_isEvEnergyRunning": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "adjust.rs:107: the dedicated EV branch is gated on process 1, fuel type 9 AND pollutant 91 together. This run's N2O and THC electricity rows do not qualify and take the standard quadratic, where `temperatureadjustment` has no row for them and the factor is exactly 1. The snapshot's ONE `temperatureadjustment` row is 9101 / fuel 9, so this predicate is exactly the set of rows the table can reach."
        },
        "rt_evTemperatureAdjustRaw": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "adjust.rs:108: (T - 72) x (A + B x (T - 72)), on the TEMPERATURE and not on the heat index. At 59.5 degF with A = 0.00225 and B = 0.00028 this is +0.015625, so the clamp below does not fire and the factor is 1.015625 -- 1.56 % on all 42 electricity energy rows, and on the Atmospheric CO2 and CO2 Equivalent rows chained off them."
        },
        "rt_batteryEfficiency": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "J33: setup.rs:3221 FORCES fuelTypeID to 9, so `evefficiency` has no fuel column and the gate is the age GROUP -- 0.950 at age group 3 down to 0.828 at 2099."
        },
        "rt_chargingEfficiency": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The charging half of the divisor, 0.94 in every row."
        },
        "rt_hasEvEfficiency": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Whether `evefficiency` carries a row for this pollutant-process at all. It does for 9101 and for nothing else, and the test is load-bearing: without it lib/onroad_activity.esm's `ev_energy_divisor` would divide this run's N2O and THC electricity rates by its own 1e-300 floor and return an infinity."
        },
        "rt_appliesEvDivisor": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
