        {
          "_comment": "S15. adjust.rs applies the fuel effects and the temperature factor to the A/C-ADJUSTED rate as well as to the base rate (they all go through `scale_base_rate`, adjust.rs:296-305) and only then adds `acFactor x acAdj`, so the factors are common to both terms and the product distributes; it is written factored, and `rt_acFactor` is exactly 0 at this hour so the two forms are not even floating-point-distinguishable. What is NEW here is where the base rate comes from: `rt_fuelFactor` already carries this row's whole speciation chain, so the rate it multiplies is the chain ROOT's. The I/M blend and the emission-rate adjustment are the two steps that follow in adjust.rs and both tables are EMPTY in this snapshot.",
