        {
          "_comment": "THE SECOND STAGE, AND WHY THERE HAS TO BE ONE. Every earlier fixture in this port computes an output row by SCALING one other row; three of this run's twenty-six SUM several. A summed row cannot be a multiplicative chain step at any depth, so it is a separate pass over the same relation -- and one pass is enough, because none of the three feeds another (docs/esm-conventions.md 40).",
          "lhs": "rtDay_quant",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "+",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "+",
                "args": [
                  "rtDay_directQuant",
                  "rtDay_totalOrganicGasesSum"
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "+",
                "args": [
                  "rtDay_co2EquivalentSum",
                  "rtDay_nonHapTogQuant"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "_comment": "The prefix count ZEROED on the rows that do not emit, so every emitting rate row has a dense 1..644 and every suppressed one has 0 (docs/esm-conventions.md 22 and 31). It is GLOBAL over the rate relation rather than per pollutant-process block, because the six blocks are not the same size: one of 124 and five of 104, and a rank built from a block offset needs every block to be the same length.",
          "lhs": "rt_outputRank",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              "rt_emits",
              "rt_prefixEmitted"
            ]
          }
        },
