        {
          "id": "the_fuel_supply_resolves_to_four_subtypes_and_the_criteria_ratio_keys_on_the_chain_root",
          "description": "S15(g). `fuelsupply` carries five rows for this region; four resolve to a fuel type through `fuelformulation.fuelSubtypeID` and `fuelsubtype.fuelTypeID`, and the fifth (28001, subtype 30) resolves to fuel type 0, matching no cohort -- an inner join that finds nothing, exactly as the port's `filter_map` drops it. THE SUBTYPES ARE WHAT THE SPECIATION KEYS ON, and none of them is its fuel type's default: gasoline is supplied as gasohol E10 (12) and not conventional gasoline (10), diesel as biodiesel blend (21) and not conventional diesel (20), ethanol as E85 (51). `criteriaratio` carries polProcessID 101 alone, so the lookup keys on the CHAIN ROOT rather than on the rate row's own pollutant-process; that is what makes `rt_fuelFactor` carry the fuel effect on a species row at all, and it is asserted at an NMHC row against the THC row's value times the methane complement. `generalfuelratio` has ZERO rows here, so its reach is 0 and the step is absent rather than inert.",
