        {
          "id": "the_E85_altTHC_branch_speciates_VOC_from_a_different_fuel_than_it_burns",
          "description": "adjust.rs:625-692 and hcspeciation.rs:715-760, and it is worth a factor of 3.85. On an ethanol cohort of model year 2001 or later, MOVES duplicates the THC block of the supplied E85 formulation, scales the copy by `altRatio / ratio` -- 1.037215919005 / 1.044099696019 = 0.99340697 at model year 2020 -- and speciates THAT into VOC using fuel subtype 12's ratios, while the emitted NMHC still comes from the ordinary block and subtype 51's ratio of 0.822. So the VOC multiplier on this cohort's THC is 0.99340697 x (1 - 0.338) x 0.974 = 0.6405369, where the ordinary path would have given (1 - 0.822) x 0.934 = 0.1662520. The five conditions are asserted separately from the arithmetic, and the model year 2000 ethanol cohort -- which has no `altcriteriaratio` row and takes the ordinary path -- is asserted beside it, because a branch that fired everywhere and a branch that fired nowhere would both be wrong and only one of them would look it.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
