        {
          "id": "the_four_air_toxic_paths_and_the_worked_examples_reach_MOVESOutput",
          "description": "`AirToxicsCalculator`'s FOUR live paths and the end of the multiplicative chain. ATRatioGas1 keys on the emission's fuel FORMULATION and on an ageID that resolves the model year -- gasoline at ageID 40 takes 0.037092331652 and at ageID 0 takes 0.047131980205, out of two windows that partition the run's model years -- and ATRatioNonGas keys on the fuel SUBTYPE and a self-described model-year group. The two cover pollutants 20, 21, 24, 25, 26 and 27 and are disjoint on every emitted cohort, so `rtSup_atRatio` is a sum of one term there; the sum is written because the Go APPENDS every path. Ethanol (21) is the one output BOTH reach, on disjoint fuel types -- gasoline through ATRatioGas1 and E85 through ATRatioNonGas -- which is why its block is 64 cohorts and not 104. The two paths this snapshot adds are minorHAPRatio, on the fuel subtype, for pollutants 40 to 46, and pahGasRatio, on the BLOCK's fuel type, for naphthalene gas (185). A zero RATIO and a missing one are different and both are asserted: 1,3-butadiene on gasoline model year 2020 has a row whose value is 0 and is emitted at 0, while every species on electricity has no row and is not emitted at all. Then twenty-five `MOVESOutput` cells, all four fuels, both day types and both ends of the model-year range, including the E85 rows the altTHC branch decides and the four cells that are exactly zero. `output_rows` is rate-major over the 2,767 emitting rate rows in blocks of two day types.",
