        {
          "id": "so2_is_the_fuel_sulfur_burned_scaled_by_the_energy_consumed",
          "description": "`SO2Calculator`, end to end. so2_calculator.rs:2079: SO2 = meanBaseRate x WsulfurLevel x energy / energyContent, where the first factor is `sulfateemissionrate` and the middle two are `SO2FuelCalculation1`'s market-share-weighted means over the county's fuel supply. Every number below except `rt_so2Factor` is a cell of an INPUT table or of MOVESOutput; `rt_so2Factor` is the port's own arithmetic and is asserted as such.\n\nThe three sulfate rates are the whole of the model-year dependence: gasoline and ethanol carry 1.99378e-06 at every model year of this run, and diesel steps from 1.89735e-06 to 1.76298e-06 at 2007 -- which is a self-described `modelYearGroupID` band, 19502006 and 20072050, decoded rather than transcribed.\n\nELECTRICITY FAILS TWICE AND BOTH FAILURES ARE ASSERTED, because either one alone would produce the same 104-cohort block and a fixture that checked one could not tell which MOVES used. `sulfateemissionrate` has no fuelTypeID 9 row, so `rt_hasSulfateRate` is 0; and fuel subtype 90's `energyContent` is NULL, so `rt_supplyEnergyContent` is 0 and the division MariaDB would evaluate as NULL is guarded. Neither is inferred from the other.\n\nThe worked example: model year 2010 gasoline on the weekday. Total Energy is 10.7536 Million BTU, which is 10.7536 x 1,055,055.9 = 1.13466e+07 kJ, and 1.13466e+07 x 3.41892e-07 = 3.879 g of SO2 -- the reference's own figure to all six digits it stores.\n\nASSERTION BY ASSERTION.\n[1] rt_supplySulfurLevel: fuelformulation 9114's `sulfurLevel`, at market share 1.0. Reference table.\n[2] rt_supplySulfurLevel: The biodiesel blend 25003's 6.0 ppm. Reference table.\n[3] rt_supplyEnergyContent: fuelsubtype 12's `energyContent`. Reference table.\n[4] rt_supplyEnergyContent: fuelsubtype 21's. Reference table.\n[5] rt_supplyEnergyContent: Subtype 90's `energyContent` is NULL and arrives as NaN; this is the port's reading of it, not the reference's, and it is what stops the SO2 division.\n[6] rt_sulfateBaseRate: Gasoline, band 19502050. Reference table.\n[7] rt_sulfateBaseRate: Diesel model year 2000, band 19502006.\n[8] rt_sulfateBaseRate: Diesel model year 2010, band 20072050 -- the step the band decoding has to find.\n[9] rt_hasSulfateRate: No fuelTypeID 9 row anywhere in `sulfateemissionrate`. The FIRST of electricity's two failures.\n[11] rt_hasSo2Factor: No SO2 row for electricity, which is what makes the block 104 cohorts and not 125.\n[12] rt_so2Factor: 1.99378e-06 x 7.15 / 41.696. THE PORT'S OWN ARITHMETIC -- MOVES materialises this in a temporary table it drops, so the snapshot does not carry it and this assertion faces this document only (docs/esm-conventions.md 35.4).\n[13] out_emissionQuant: Model year 2010 gasoline, weekday. MOVESOutput.\n[14] out_emissionQuant: Model year 2000 diesel, weekday -- the cell that reads the 19502006 band. MOVESOutput.\n[15] out_emissionQuant: The Total Energy Consumption the cell above is computed from, in Million BTU. It is asserted here because the SO2 factor is dimensionless in kilojoules and a reader has to see both ends of the conversion to check the example by hand.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "tolerance": {
            "rel": 2e-05
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "rt_supplySulfurLevel",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 7.15,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 1487
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rt_supplySulfurLevel",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 6.0,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 1528
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rt_supplyEnergyContent",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 41.696,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 1487
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rt_supplyEnergyContent",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 42.7,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 1528
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rt_supplyEnergyContent",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 1610
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rt_sulfateBaseRate",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.99378e-06,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 1487
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rt_sulfateBaseRate",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.89735e-06,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 1538
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rt_sulfateBaseRate",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.76298e-06,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 1528
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rt_hasSulfateRate",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 1610
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rt_hasSo2Factor",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.0,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 1487
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rt_hasSo2Factor",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 1610
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rt_so2Factor",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 3.4189195606293174e-07,
              "coords": {
