        {
          "id": "nonhaptog_is_nmog_minus_the_mechanisms_integrated_species",
          "description": "`TOGSpeciationCalculator`, and the two things about it a passing comparison would not say.\n\nFIRST, WHAT MAKES THIS SNAPSHOT THE ONE. The calculator is class-loaded in ALL 42 snapshots of the corpus, because `ExecutionRunSpec` calls its static `needsFinalAggregation()`, so loading is no evidence at all that it ran. What discriminates is `integratedspeciesset`: 14 rows here and ZERO in every other snapshot, including the one named `chain-tog-speciation`. Its fourteen pollutants are exactly this run's fourteen air toxics, and `run_integratedSpeciesMechanismSpread` pins that they are all one mechanism -- which is also the LIMIT of this fixture, because the per-(mechanism, set) fan-out of togspeciation.rs's step 2 has one member here and a second mechanism would double-count if the join were wrong.\n\nSECOND, THE CLAMP IS NOT CHECKED HERE. `greatest(sum(...), 0)` is the calculator's whole protection against a speciation that over-subtracts, and on all 208 emitted cells of this run the residual is positive: the fourteen species take between 16.1 % and 48.6 % of NMOG. `rtDay_nonHapTogRaw` is asserted equal to `rtDay_nonHapTogQuant` at the smallest residual in the run, which is the honest statement that the clamp is a no-op here (docs/esm-conventions.md 23).\n\nThe worked example: model year 2010 gasoline on the weekday. NMOG is 41.7547 g, the fourteen species sum to 10.853 g, and NonHAPTOG is 30.9017 g -- MOVESOutput's figure. TOG is checked in the same test because it is the other sum this document forms and it shares the machinery: 41.7547 + 20.5384 = 62.2932 g, NMOG plus methane, and on the twenty ethanol cohorts of model year 2001 or later those two summands come from different blocks.\n\nASSERTION BY ASSERTION.\n[1] run_integratedSpeciesMechanismSpread: One mechanism. The number that says what this fixture does NOT check.\n[2] run_integratedSpeciesMechanismMax: `integratedspeciesset.mechanismID`, the CB05 mechanism 5.\n[4] rt_isTotalOrganicGases: The three summed pollutants are disjoint.\n[5] rtDay_nonHapTogNmog: The POSITIVE term: the NMOG row of the same cell, which the SQL synthesises into the integrated-species set with a + sign. MOVESOutput's NMOG figure.\n[6] rtDay_nonHapTogSpecies: The fourteen species subtracted. It is a DIFFERENCE of two MOVESOutput figures -- 41.7547 - 30.9017 -- so it carries only four significant digits of the reference and its tolerance says so rather than pretending to six.\n[7] rtDay_nonHapTogRaw: Before the clamp.\n[8] rtDay_nonHapTogQuant: After it, and EQUAL, because no cell of this run is negative. The clamp is written because the source writes it and is checked nowhere here.\n[9] out_emissionQuant: NonHAPTOG, model year 2010 gasoline, weekday. MOVESOutput.\n[10] out_emissionQuant: Its NMOG parent. MOVESOutput.\n[11] out_emissionQuant: TOG for the same cell: NMOG 41.7547 + methane 20.5384. MOVESOutput.\n[12] out_emissionQuant: The methane half of that TOG. MOVESOutput.",
